# UC-01 authorship rule (#179).
#
# A drawing must have an author. The ontology cannot say so: under the open-world assumption a minimum cardinality
# on isAuthoredBy would infer an author nobody extracted instead of reporting that none was recorded (#84). So the rule
# is a closed-world check on DATA, and it is the answer to competency question CQ 4.4 of the UC-01 ORSD ("which drawings
# have no recorded author?"). What is read here is documented in docs/contribute/data-validation.md.
#
# A drawing that records no author of its own is read as authored by the authors of its revisions, so an author on any
# revision satisfies the rule (the path below). A drawing's own author is not replaced by a revision's: this is a reading
# convention, not an entailment.
#
# Only the author is required. A drawing may or may not have been checked or approved, so a checker and an approver are
# optional and no rule reports their absence.
#
# Severity: sh:Warning. A drawing with no recorded author is incomplete, not malformed, and the report cannot say why
# (the extraction missed it, or the drawing names none): telling those apart is the vocabulary of #187.

@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix metadata: <https://w3id.org/adiro/adiro_drawing_metadata#> .
@prefix dv: <https://w3id.org/adiro/data-validation/uc01-authorship#> .

dv:DrawingAuthor a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass metadata:DrawingSheet ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path [ sh:alternativePath ( metadata:isAuthoredBy ( metadata:hasRevision metadata:isAuthoredBy ) ) ] ;
        sh:severity sh:Warning ;  # a property shape does not inherit the severity of its node shape
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:message "A drawing has at least one recorded author."
    ] .
